WEBVTT

00:01.937 --> 00:09.219
[SPEAKER_01]: Third of Wealsun, Merrick has just come into the barracks and heard the end of Folsom's disastrous song.

00:12.420 --> 00:13.001
[SPEAKER_00]: You're shocked.

00:13.681 --> 00:15.401
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm not too happy right now.

00:16.362 --> 00:18.682
[SPEAKER_01]: Because this is exactly what you were told to avoid.

00:22.083 --> 00:28.005
[SPEAKER_01]: Gouge takes Folsom outside and you're a little worried he's gonna stab the kid and throw him in a...

00:28.860 --> 00:29.200
[SPEAKER_01]: Me too.

00:29.360 --> 00:30.021
[SPEAKER_01]: Me too.

00:30.041 --> 00:31.062
[SPEAKER_01]: Throw him in an alleyway.

00:31.442 --> 00:37.527
[SPEAKER_01]: But you see Owen Black up against the bar going, laughing and drinking right next to Tyrus.

00:37.547 --> 00:39.989
[SPEAKER_01]: He goes, what happened to Folsom?

00:41.009 --> 00:42.971
[SPEAKER_01]: That must have been rough on our whole mind.

00:45.738 --> 00:46.539
[SPEAKER_02]: It's a farce.

00:47.060 --> 00:48.922
[SPEAKER_02]: It was meant to be a farce, a joke.

00:49.643 --> 00:51.785
[SPEAKER_02]: Kid always tries to crack jokes.

00:52.085 --> 00:52.766
[SPEAKER_02]: I keep telling him.

00:52.786 --> 00:53.527
[SPEAKER_02]: It's not working.

00:53.607 --> 00:55.950
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, you should tell him Marines don't like jokes.

00:56.010 --> 00:57.592
[SPEAKER_01]: Especially not when it's about them.

00:57.752 --> 00:58.653
[SPEAKER_02]: You know what Marines like?

00:59.073 --> 00:59.554
[SPEAKER_02]: Beer!

01:00.655 --> 01:02.437
[SPEAKER_00]: And put my gold on the table there.

01:04.887 --> 01:09.548
[SPEAKER_00]: Kevin looks like I came in at a wrong time.

01:09.809 --> 01:11.769
[SPEAKER_00]: That song, was that for In My Favor?

01:11.789 --> 01:13.670
[SPEAKER_00]: You guys put that on for me when I came in?

01:13.850 --> 01:14.690
[SPEAKER_02]: Not at all.

01:14.970 --> 01:17.551
[SPEAKER_02]: Did you talk to him at all?

01:18.671 --> 01:23.593
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, so, I'm gonna see you later, buddy.

01:23.633 --> 01:24.313
[SPEAKER_02]: Good to see you, Owen.

01:24.433 --> 01:24.993
[SPEAKER_02]: I'll talk to...

01:25.213 --> 01:26.974
[SPEAKER_02]: I think we all owe a full small word after this.

01:26.994 --> 01:27.574
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah, yeah.

01:27.754 --> 01:31.035
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, I gotta talk, I gotta report to my captain, so...

01:32.691 --> 01:33.512
[SPEAKER_03]: I'm bailing from the bar.

01:33.672 --> 01:35.474
[SPEAKER_02]: Was that Gouge in the bar?

01:35.655 --> 01:37.136
[SPEAKER_03]: I have no idea who that guy was.

01:38.258 --> 01:40.080
[SPEAKER_02]: Why'd you let him take your friend out?

01:40.120 --> 01:40.781
[SPEAKER_03]: I'll see you later.

01:41.021 --> 01:41.702
[SPEAKER_03]: I'm out the bar.

01:41.822 --> 01:42.443
[SPEAKER_03]: I'm out the door.

01:42.463 --> 01:44.165
[SPEAKER_03]: Because I don't know what Gouge is going to be.

01:44.185 --> 01:45.147
[SPEAKER_03]: Okay, so you're going to leave.

01:45.227 --> 01:45.868
[SPEAKER_00]: What do you want to do?

01:46.048 --> 01:47.350
[SPEAKER_00]: I'll talk to Owen for a second.

01:47.470 --> 01:49.352
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay, so you go, and they'll talk.

01:53.372 --> 01:55.593
[SPEAKER_01]: That was a show.

01:55.653 --> 01:56.853
[SPEAKER_00]: Strange circumstances.

01:57.293 --> 01:57.893
[SPEAKER_00]: Absolutely.

01:57.913 --> 01:58.593
[SPEAKER_00]: Good to see you.

01:58.613 --> 01:59.893
[SPEAKER_00]: Hope your travels have been good.

02:00.874 --> 02:02.534
[SPEAKER_00]: Good to see you in one piece as well.

02:05.295 --> 02:06.535
[SPEAKER_00]: I mean, you know, how's it been?

02:07.755 --> 02:08.335
[SPEAKER_01]: It's been good.

02:08.395 --> 02:09.015
[SPEAKER_01]: Stay busy?

02:09.095 --> 02:09.696
[SPEAKER_01]: Absolutely.

02:09.736 --> 02:11.036
[SPEAKER_01]: Just got back from Red Shore.

02:11.516 --> 02:11.876
[SPEAKER_01]: Awesome.

02:11.956 --> 02:12.696
[SPEAKER_01]: Made quite a haul.

02:12.736 --> 02:16.677
[SPEAKER_01]: That's where all the merchants have been stuck by the Duke of Gradsall, by the way.

02:16.737 --> 02:20.878
[SPEAKER_01]: I was able to load up the skiff, make it back with quite a bit of food.

02:21.729 --> 02:22.270
[SPEAKER_01]: Have a drink.

02:22.350 --> 02:22.830
[SPEAKER_01]: It's full.

02:23.772 --> 02:25.754
[SPEAKER_01]: Not watered-down ale or anything like that.

02:25.774 --> 02:26.134
[SPEAKER_01]: Perfect.

02:26.455 --> 02:27.696
[SPEAKER_01]: Perfect.

02:27.997 --> 02:29.879
[SPEAKER_00]: Care if I join you for a drink really quick?

02:30.099 --> 02:30.600
[SPEAKER_01]: Not at all.

02:30.960 --> 02:31.561
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll buy you one.

02:32.162 --> 02:33.383
[SPEAKER_01]: I'd be all free anyway.

02:33.403 --> 02:34.605
[SPEAKER_00]: I appreciate it.

02:34.845 --> 02:38.830
[SPEAKER_00]: After a performance like that, I think I need to clear my mind a little bit.

02:40.251 --> 02:40.892
[SPEAKER_00]: Red Shore, you say?

02:40.972 --> 02:41.232
[SPEAKER_00]: Busy?

02:43.062 --> 02:44.904
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, 50 merchant ships there.

02:46.185 --> 02:47.086
[SPEAKER_01]: They can't unload them.

02:47.226 --> 02:48.327
[SPEAKER_01]: They don't have the docks for it.

02:48.747 --> 02:50.549
[SPEAKER_01]: You've been to Red Shore, you know what it looks like.

02:50.589 --> 02:51.970
[SPEAKER_01]: It's a whaling town.

02:52.210 --> 02:52.550
[SPEAKER_01]: Of course.

02:52.570 --> 02:55.913
[SPEAKER_01]: They have a hard time unloading ships, I mean, fishing ships.

02:56.554 --> 02:58.996
[SPEAKER_01]: But merchant ships, they can't do it.

02:59.016 --> 03:00.517
[SPEAKER_01]: They're all there languishing.

03:01.378 --> 03:04.901
[SPEAKER_01]: Full of food that's rotting, full of goods that are not being sold.

03:06.662 --> 03:10.546
[SPEAKER_01]: Duke of Gradsul is making a mess of it.

03:11.845 --> 03:12.505
[SPEAKER_01]: Sounds like it.

03:14.346 --> 03:16.866
[SPEAKER_01]: But my profit, to my profit, absolutely.

03:18.107 --> 03:18.567
[SPEAKER_01]: Good.

03:20.107 --> 03:20.607
[SPEAKER_00]: Very good.

03:24.228 --> 03:25.489
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

03:26.989 --> 03:29.009
[SPEAKER_00]: When did you get back from, what did you say, Red Farm?

03:29.550 --> 03:29.970
[SPEAKER_01]: Red Shore.

03:30.350 --> 03:31.550
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, when did you get back from Red Shore?

03:32.150 --> 03:32.490
[SPEAKER_01]: Today.

03:32.750 --> 03:33.551
[SPEAKER_00]: Just got back today?

03:33.611 --> 03:33.851
[SPEAKER_01]: Noon.

03:34.311 --> 03:34.731
[SPEAKER_00]: Interesting.

03:36.820 --> 03:41.504
[SPEAKER_01]: I talked to Tyrus about the sahaugin that were in the bay, actually.

03:41.524 --> 03:42.746
[SPEAKER_01]: A couple of them attacked us.

03:43.553 --> 03:45.054
[SPEAKER_01]: Have you seen Sahaugin all the way out there?

03:45.774 --> 03:50.837
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, I was five miles from the city, that's when they attacked us.

03:50.877 --> 03:51.658
[SPEAKER_01]: Monmurg or Red Shore?

03:51.998 --> 03:52.298
[SPEAKER_01]: Monmurg.

03:53.399 --> 03:53.639
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay.

03:53.779 --> 03:58.282
[SPEAKER_00]: I've seen Sahaugin, though, on the coast of Selenmore, up near Red Shore.

03:58.302 --> 03:58.962
[SPEAKER_00]: That makes sense.

03:59.042 --> 04:04.626
[SPEAKER_00]: I think some of my men have been running in Sahaugin as well, which is very unlike.

04:04.646 --> 04:05.646
[SPEAKER_00]: We haven't seen them in years.

04:05.886 --> 04:06.647
[SPEAKER_01]: They're coming back.

04:06.827 --> 04:07.107
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

04:07.187 --> 04:08.868
[SPEAKER_00]: No, something strange is going on.

04:10.809 --> 04:11.330
[SPEAKER_00]: Any of your men?

04:12.537 --> 04:13.218
[SPEAKER_00]: Get hurt on the way?

04:14.298 --> 04:14.719
[SPEAKER_00]: Two died.

04:15.379 --> 04:16.440
[SPEAKER_00]: Sahaugin?

04:17.321 --> 04:18.582
[SPEAKER_00]: It was the Sahaugin, yes.

04:18.882 --> 04:20.323
[SPEAKER_00]: Any other trouble besides the Sahaugin?

04:21.224 --> 04:21.824
[SPEAKER_01]: Not really.

04:23.125 --> 04:24.887
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm almost as good as a pilot as you.

04:24.907 --> 04:26.848
[SPEAKER_01]: I was able to avoid the patrols.

04:26.868 --> 04:27.248
[SPEAKER_00]: Of course.

04:27.769 --> 04:33.873
[SPEAKER_00]: I trust your navigational skills are probably traveling a lot more lately.

04:33.913 --> 04:35.114
[SPEAKER_00]: Probably increasing.

04:35.455 --> 04:35.835
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

04:36.822 --> 04:42.444
[SPEAKER_01]: However, I think the only other person that can make it through the patrols and get to Red Shore besides me is you.

04:42.464 --> 04:43.004
[SPEAKER_01]: Of course.

04:43.865 --> 04:44.605
[SPEAKER_01]: We both know this.

04:44.885 --> 04:46.506
[SPEAKER_01]: What do you think about going into business?

04:46.626 --> 04:48.787
[SPEAKER_01]: Quitting this foolishness in the Marines?

04:50.207 --> 04:51.308
[SPEAKER_00]: The city needs ya.

04:52.088 --> 04:52.688
[SPEAKER_00]: This is true.

04:53.788 --> 04:56.289
[SPEAKER_00]: And politics are getting a little old around here.

04:56.590 --> 04:58.050
[SPEAKER_00]: Not sure what's going on, per se.

04:58.830 --> 05:03.192
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, according to your friend over there, the princes are all fools.

05:03.732 --> 05:05.613
[SPEAKER_00]: According to him, the princes are all fools.

05:08.730 --> 05:12.152
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm not here to make any negotiating answers.

05:12.193 --> 05:17.717
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm here to have a drink and catch up with my cousin and apparently get mocked to by some bard.

05:18.417 --> 05:24.682
[SPEAKER_00]: So yes, Owen, that was Gouch who was here.

05:27.023 --> 05:28.364
[SPEAKER_01]: You think you can get him on your crew?

05:30.066 --> 05:31.407
[SPEAKER_00]: Gouch, for the right coin.

05:32.743 --> 05:33.884
[SPEAKER_00]: Or the right amount of red-eye.

05:34.084 --> 05:37.186
[SPEAKER_01]: He'd be very useful out there on the sea if he wanted that.

05:37.487 --> 05:37.887
[SPEAKER_01]: He would.

05:38.567 --> 05:40.349
[SPEAKER_01]: I was thinking about hiring him myself.

05:40.429 --> 05:42.330
[SPEAKER_01]: I know him by reputation, definitely.

05:42.570 --> 05:57.522
[SPEAKER_01]: And in fact, about a week ago, I took a compatriot of his, this elf, from Red Shore to Essar.

05:58.387 --> 06:03.932
[SPEAKER_01]: That's a small fishing town on the north coast of the sea principalities.

06:04.233 --> 06:08.156
[SPEAKER_01]: Tell them to get me in touch with Gouch.

06:08.197 --> 06:11.340
[SPEAKER_01]: I think if we hire these mercenaries, we can do well for ourselves.

06:12.220 --> 06:12.881
[SPEAKER_01]: This is true.

06:13.101 --> 06:16.484
[SPEAKER_01]: It's dangerous out there, but... What are you smuggling nowadays?

06:16.545 --> 06:19.607
[SPEAKER_00]: What's your... Well, food seems to be the most important thing.

06:20.849 --> 06:21.990
[SPEAKER_00]: As I would think.

06:22.923 --> 06:24.124
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, you know, that could be drawn in.

06:24.764 --> 06:27.426
[SPEAKER_00]: Sahaugin, too, if they smell stuff they're transporting, too.

06:27.466 --> 06:27.967
[SPEAKER_00]: It's dangerous.

06:28.727 --> 06:28.907
[SPEAKER_00]: Yep.

06:29.227 --> 06:29.828
[SPEAKER_00]: Very dangerous.

06:29.928 --> 06:34.031
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, Owen, you have me intrigued, for sure.

06:35.512 --> 06:38.113
[SPEAKER_00]: And, you know, I always have your best interests in mind.

06:38.134 --> 06:39.795
[SPEAKER_01]: Now, go say that, boy.

06:39.855 --> 06:40.875
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what I'm out for.

06:41.496 --> 06:42.677
[SPEAKER_00]: I'm afraid Gouge is gonna kill him.

06:42.697 --> 06:44.458
[SPEAKER_00]: I want to make sure Gouge doesn't do anything out of it.

06:44.578 --> 06:45.118
[SPEAKER_00]: Absolutely.

06:46.079 --> 06:48.721
[SPEAKER_01]: Proposition him, though, and I can get you another boat.

06:49.421 --> 06:51.843
[SPEAKER_01]: We can do this right, and we can make a lot of money.

06:53.053 --> 06:53.576
[SPEAKER_00]: Sounds good, Owen.

06:53.616 --> 06:53.938
[SPEAKER_01]: Thank you.

